  "generated_text": "To solve the problem, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the variables:**\n   Let \\( A \\), \\( B \\), and \\( C \\) be the values of the variables.\n\n2. **Set up the given conditions:**\n   - The arithmetic mean of \\( A \\), \\( B \\), and \\( C \\) is 10.\n   - \\( A \\) is six less than \\( B \\).\n   - \\( C \\) is three more than \\( B \\).\n\n3. **Translate the conditions into equations:**\n   - The arithmetic mean condition gives us:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{A + B + C}{3} = 10\n     \\]\n     Multiplying both sides by 3:\n     \\[\n     A + B + C = 30\n     \\]\n   - The relationship between \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) is:\n     \\[\n     A = B - 6\n     \\]\n   - The relationship between \\( C \\) and \\( B \\) is:\n     \\[\n     C = B + 3\n     \\]\n\n4. **Substitute the expressions for \\( A \\) and \\( C \\) into the mean equation:**\n   Substitute \\( A = B - 6 \\) and \\( C = B + 3 \\) into \\( A + B + C = 30 \\):\n   \\[\n   (B - 6) + B + (B + 3) = 30\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the equation:**\n   Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   B - 6 + B + B + 3 = 30\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3B - 3 = 30\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for \\( B \\):**\n   Add 3 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   3B = 33\n   \\]\n   Divide by 3:\n   \\[\n   B = 11\n   \\]\n\n7. **Find the value of \\( C \\):**\n   Using \\( C = B + 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   C = 11 + 3 = 14\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( C \\) is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
